  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "North American West Coast Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP) data, 1996-present",
  "description": "Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler data from many local and international locations. Largely experimental data collected in development of instrumentation. May be coordinated with other data collected, such as CTD, current meters, echo soundings, and meteorological buoys. Frequently collected in collaboration with other institutions.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Study of upper ocean processes, wave breaking, bubbles, turbulence\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Principal investigator has left DFO, but the data are secure. Data are in electronic format, well backed up and well documented. Risk of Loss: Low Impact Justification: Data used for one time analysis. Data from experiments or data generated from models. Impact of Loss: Low Recommended Action: None",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570789",
